  "raw": {
    "https://gustavus.edu/employment/job/2434": {
      "title": "Instructor of the Practice (Finance) - Part Time - Business and Economics",
      "description": "Instructor of the Practice (Finance) - Part Time - Business and Economics It appears you have javascript disabled. Please enable javascript to get the full experience of gustavus.edu Skip to Main Content Skip to Footer Sign In Gustavus Adolphus College Make Your Life Count Gustavus Adolphus College Instructor of the Practice (Finance) - Part Time Business and Economics Home Openings : 1 Description Gustavus Adolphus College invites applications for a part-time, one-semester position of Instructor of the Practice (or Assistant Professor of the Practice with appropriate qualifications) in the Department of Business and Economics to begin January 1, 2027. The department anticipates a continued vacancy, and the successful candidate may be considered for continuation into the following academic year, contingent upon favorable review and the continuing needs of the College. Applicants must have current authorization to work in the United States. Gustavus will not sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa for this position. Gustavus is not an e-verify institution. Employment Type: Part-Time; $5,000 per 4-credit course (a total of $10,000 for two courses); Exempt (Salaried); In-Person Instruction Prerequisites Required Qualifications MBA, MAcc, MBT, or equivalent, but we will consider candidates with significant professional experience (PhD or ABD preferred) Demonstrated ability to teach, train, or mentor others Ability to teach Managerial Finance and Investments Preferred Qualifications Evidence of effectiveness in teaching Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate students Demonstrated commitment to supporting students from diverse backgrounds and identities Prior experience in corporate finance, banking, investment management, financial planning, venture capital, private equity, financial analysis, entrepreneurship, or a related field Position Overview Teach 2 course sections in the 2027 spring semester. Primary teaching responsibilities will include Managerial Finance and Investments, although the final courses assigned will be determined based on the candidate’s preparation, interests, and departmental needs. Responsibilities: Your role will go beyond the textbook. You'll use your real-world experience to help students connect financial concepts with professional decision-making and develop the analytical, technological, and communication skills needed for changing careers and industries. Help cultivate a welcoming community where everyone feels a sense of belonging. We strive to foster an environment where people can be themselves, build community, learn, and grow. Why Teach at Gustavus? Mentor the next generation of financial professionals. This position offers a unique chance to mentor bright, engaged students. As part of a community committed to fostering belonging and purpose, you’ll have the flexibility to balance your professional and personal life while shaping future leaders. Elevate your teaching. Take advantage of opportunities to join a teaching circle, participate in workshops, apply for an internal teaching development grant, and engage in conversations about teaching with colleagues across campus. Develop professional skills by participating in faculty meetings and committees, attending faculty development days, and taking advantage of the College’s membership to the National Center for Faculty Development and Diversity (NCFDD). Be a part of our community. We offer free parking, exercise classes, and use of library and athletic facilities. How to Apply To apply, visit https://gustavus.edu/jobs/ and complete the online application. The documents that must be uploaded include the following: Letter of application Curriculum vitae or professional résumé A brief (one page) statement of teaching philosophy Transcripts (scanned copies acceptable) The names and contact information for three professional references (at least one must be able to address teaching experience and teaching effectiveness; please indicate the teaching reference in your letter of application). Please do not ask references to submit letters of recommendation; the committee will conduct reference checks by phone. The letter of application should identify the courses the candidate is prepared to teach and explain how the candidate’s academic or professional experience would benefit Gustavus students. Applicants whose primary experience is outside higher education may use the teaching statement to discuss relevant mentoring, training, supervision, presentation, or professional-development experience. Applications will be reviewed beginning September 15, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled with the goal to fill this position by early November. Incomplete applications will not be considered. The first-round interviews will be held online. Institution Information Gustavus Adolphus College is one of the nation’s leading private liberal arts colleges serving 1,800 students, where faculty help equip students to lead purposeful lives and to act on the great challenges of our time. The College aspires to be a community of persons from diverse backgrounds who respect and affirm the dignity of all people. Gustavus is located on a scenic 340-acre hill in St. Peter, Minnesota, and within a short drive to the Minneapolis/Saint Paul and Mankato metro areas. Learn more at https://gustavus.edu/about/administrative-offices/provost/prospective-faculty-provost . Gustavus Adolphus College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, disability, religion, age, sexual orientation, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Department Information The Department of Business and Economics is one of Gustavus’s largest and fastest-growing departments. Its programs in business management, economics, accounting, and financial economics prepare students for professional success, leadership, and thoughtful citizenship through rigorous, applied, interdisciplinary, and student-centered education. The department emphasizes applied, data-driven, and experiential education. Courses incorporate real-world financial data, financial modeling, cases, simulations, projects, and engagement with finance professionals. For more information, visit the departmental website: https://gustavus.edu/academics/departments/business-and-economics . NOTE: Candidates will not be compensated for materials prepared as part of the interview process, and the College will not retain the materials for its own use. Contact Cathy Harms | charms@gustavus.edu | 507-933-7414 Posted : Tue Aug 18, 2026 Apply Now 800 West College Avenue Saint Peter, MN 56082 507-933-8000 © 2026 Gustavus Adolphus College Careers Feedback Privacy Statement Title IX"
    },
    "https://gustavus.edu/employment/job/2451": {
      "title": "Visiting Instructor (Economics) - Part Time - Business and Economics",
      "description": "Visiting Instructor (Economics) - Part Time - Business and Economics It appears you have javascript disabled. Please enable javascript to get the full experience of gustavus.edu Skip to Main Content Skip to Footer Sign In Gustavus Adolphus College Make Your Life Count Gustavus Adolphus College Visiting Instructor (Economics) - Part Time Business and Economics Home Openings : 1 Description Gustavus Adolphus College invites applications for a one course sabbatical replacement position of Visiting Instructor (or Visiting Assistant Professor with appropriate qualifications) in the Department of Business and Economics, starting January 2027. Applicants must have current authorization to work in the United States. Gustavus will not sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa for this position. Gustavus is not an e-verify institution. Employment Type: Part-Time; $5,000 per 4-credit course; Exempt (Salaried); In-Person Instruction. Prerequisites Required Qualifications Master’s degree in economics or a related field (PhD or ABD preferred) Preferred Qualifications Evidence of effectiveness in teaching Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate students Demonstrated commitment to supporting students from diverse backgrounds and identities Position Overview Teach 1 course section in the 2027 spring semester. The teaching responsibility will be one upper-level economics elective, drawn from departmental needs and the candidate’s expertise, with particular interest in health economics. The will meet either M-W-F for 65 minutes each day or T-Th 95 minutes class each day. Help cultivate a welcoming community where everyone feels a sense of belonging. We strive to foster an environment where people can be themselves, build community, learn, and grow. Why Teach at Gustavus? Elevate your teaching. Take advantage of opportunities to join a teaching circle, participate in workshops, apply for an internal teaching development grant, and engage in conversations about teaching with colleagues across campus. Develop professional skills by participating in faculty meetings and committees, attending faculty development days, and taking advantage of the College’s membership to the National Center for Faculty Development and Diversity (NCFDD). Be a part of our community. We offer free parking, exercise classes, and use of library and athletic facilities. How to Apply To apply, visit https://gustavus.edu/jobs/ and complete the online application. The documents that must be uploaded include the following: Letter of application that addresses the position qualifications Curriculum vitae A brief (one page) statement of teaching philosophy Transcripts (scanned copies acceptable) The names and contact information for three professional references (at least one must be able to address teaching experience and teaching effectiveness; please indicate the teaching reference in your letter of application). Please do not ask references to submit letters of recommendation; the committee will conduct reference checks by phone. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. At this time, please only upload the required documents listed above; finalists may be asked to submit additional materials as needed. Incomplete applications will not be considered by the search committee. Institution Information Gustavus Adolphus College is one of the nation’s leading private liberal arts colleges serving 1,800 students, where faculty help equip students to lead purposeful lives and to act on the great challenges of our time. The College aspires to be a community of persons from diverse backgrounds who respect and affirm the dignity of all people. Gustavus is located on a scenic 340-acre hill in St. Peter, Minnesota, and within a short drive to the Minneapolis/Saint Paul and Mankato metro areas. Learn more at https://gustavus.edu/about/administrative-offices/provost/prospective-faculty-provost . Gustavus Adolphus College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, disability, religion, age, sexual orientation, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Department Information The Department of Business and Economics is one of Gustavus’s largest and fastest-growing departments. Its programs in business management, economics, accounting, and financial economics prepare students for professional success, leadership, and thoughtful citizenship through rigorous, applied, interdisciplinary, and student-centered education. The department emphasizes applied, data-driven, and experiential education. Courses incorporate real-world financial data, financial modeling, cases, simulations, projects, and engagement with finance professionals. For more information, visit the departmental website: https://gustavus.edu/academics/departments/business-and-economics . NOTE: Candidates will not be compensated for materials prepared as part of the interview process, and the College will not retain the materials for its own use. Contact Cathy Harms | charms@gustavus.edu | 507-933-7414 Posted : Thu Oct 1, 2026 Apply Now 800 West College Avenue Saint Peter, MN 56082 507-933-8000 © 2026 Gustavus Adolphus College Careers Feedback Privacy Statement Title IX"
