    "https://gustavus.edu/employment/job/2420": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (GIS and Global Health) - Environment, Geography, and Earth Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (GIS and Global Health) - Environment, Geography, and Earth Sciences It appears you have javascript disabled. Please enable javascript to get the full experience of gustavus.edu Skip to Main Content Skip to Footer Sign In Gustavus Adolphus College Make Your Life Count Gustavus Adolphus College Assistant Professor (GIS and Global Health) Environment, Geography, and Earth Sciences Home Openings : 1 Description Position Details: Gustavus Adolphus College invites applications for a tenure-track position of Assistant Professor in the Department of Environment, Geography, and Earth Sciences to begin August 15, 2027. Employment Type: Full-Time (1.0 FTE), Benefits-Eligible; Exempt (Salaried) Prerequisites Position Details: Gustavus Adolphus College invites applications for a tenure-track position of Assistant Professor in the Department of Environment, Geography, and Earth Sciences to begin August 15, 2027. Employment Type: Full-Time (1.0 FTE), Benefits-Eligible; Exempt (Salaried) Required Qualifications: PhD in Geography (or a related field); we will consider candidates who have achieved ABD status and who will complete their degree by September 30, 2027 Expertise in GIS Ability to teach courses in GIS (using ArcGIS Pro) and a course in health geography Active research agenda in geography or related field Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated effectiveness in teaching Active research agenda in GIS and global health Evidence of a commitment to undergraduate student advising Demonstrated commitment to supporting students from varied backgrounds and identities Things you will do: Gustavus faculty teach, advise, conduct research, and serve the college and department. Teach a 6-course equivalent each academic year. In their first year, the successful candidate will receive a reduced teaching assignment of five courses, plus one fully-compensated course release. Courses may be different sections of the same course within a semester. Primary teaching responsibilities will include introductory and advanced geospatial courses, a course in health geography, and contributions to general education. Help cultivate a welcoming community where everyone feels a sense of belonging. We strive to foster an environment where people can be themselves, build community, learn, and grow. Elevate your teaching by joining a teaching circle, participating in workshops, applying for an internal teaching development grant, and engaging in conversations about teaching with colleagues across campus. Advance your scholarship by working with undergraduate research assistants, joining a writing retreat, applying for an internal grant, receiving travel funds to present at conferences, receiving help applying for external grants, and making use of our research facilities. Develop professional skills by participating in faculty meetings and committees, attending faculty development days, and taking advantage of the College’s membership to the National Center for Faculty Development and Diversity (NCFDD). How to apply: Visit https://gustavus.edu/jobs/ and complete the online application. The documents that must be uploaded include the following: Letter of application that addresses the required and preferred position qualifications Curriculum vitae A brief (one page) statement of your teaching philosophy and practices A brief (one page) statement of research areas and future research directions A brief (one page) statement of ways in which you cultivate a welcoming community through teaching, scholarship, service, and/or advising/mentoring Graduate transcripts (scanned copies acceptable) The names and contact information for three professional references (at least one must be able to address teaching experience and teaching effectiveness; please indicate the teaching reference in your letter of application). Please do not ask references to submit letters of recommendation; the committee will conduct reference checks by phone. For full consideration, applications must be received by Monday, September 14, 2026. While applications may be accepted after this date, it is not guaranteed that they will be considered. At this time, please only upload the required documents listed above; finalists may be asked to submit additional materials. Incomplete applications will not be considered by the search committee. Things you’ll like: Based on data from AAUP (American Association of University Professors) and CUPA (College and University Professional Association), we offer a competitive starting salary range of $66,000 to $72,000 for a 9-month academic year. Actual pay will be adjusted based on job-related factors permitted by law, such as experience, training, certifications/licensure, market factors, departmental budgets, and responsibility. In addition, Gustavus provides comprehensive benefits designed to support your personal and financial well-being, including: Medical insurance (which includes access to Nice Healthcare) as well as dental, vision, and life insurance Workplace accommodations for physical or mental health concerns Access to mental health apps Onsite health services Free parking, exercise classes, use of library and athletic facilities Paid parental leave (after one year of employment) Employer contribution to retirement savings plan (after one year of employment) Tuition scholarships for dependents Tuition benefit plan for employees and spouse Institution Information: Gustavus Adolphus College is one of the nation’s leading private liberal arts colleges serving 2,000 students, where faculty help equip students to lead purposeful lives and to act on the great challenges of our time. The College aspires to be a community of persons from diverse backgrounds who respect and affirm the dignity of all people. Gustavus is located on a scenic 340-acre hill in St. Peter, Minnesota, and within a short drive to the Minneapolis/Saint Paul and Mankato metro areas. Learn more at https://gustavus.edu/provost/newfaculty/ . Gustavus Adolphus College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, disability, religion, age, sexual orientation, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Department Information: The Department of Environment, Geography, and Earth Sciences (EGE) is a transdisciplinary community of learners engaged with the challenges of living on a changing planet Earth. EGE brings together the traditional disciplines of Geography and Geology with the interdisciplinary field of Environmental Studies into a single, interdisciplinary department that seeks to understand our planetary home from a variety of perspectives. Students in the department may seek majors/minors in Environmental Studies (ENV), Geography (GEG), or Geology (GEO), and EGE faculty may be fully or jointly appointed in the department. For more information about the department, its faculty, students, and courses, please see the department website at https://gustavus.edu/ege/ . The Public Health Program focuses on addressing challenges that impact the health status of communities and individuals such as accessing health care, tools for controlling infectious diseases, environmental health, substance abuse and violence, and more. The program prepares Gusties to advocate for public health initiatives in a wide range of professional fields at the global, state, and county levels, or to work in nonprofit leadership, healthcare, and business. For more information about the program, its faculty, students, and courses, please see the program website at https://gustavus.edu/academics/departments/public-health . NOTE: Candidates will not be compensated for materials prepared as part of the interview process, and the College will not retain the materials for its own use. Contact Anna Versluis | averslui@gustavus.edu | 507-933-6058 Posted : Mon Jun 29, 2026 Apply Now 800 West College Avenue Saint Peter, MN 56082 507-933-8000 © 2026 Gustavus Adolphus College Careers Feedback Privacy Statement Title IX"
    },
    "https://gustavus.edu/employment/job/2419": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Statistics) - Mathematics, Computer Science, and Statistics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Statistics) - Mathematics, Computer Science, and Statistics It appears you have javascript disabled. Please enable javascript to get the full experience of gustavus.edu Skip to Main Content Skip to Footer Sign In Gustavus Adolphus College Make Your Life Count Gustavus Adolphus College Assistant Professor (Statistics) Mathematics, Computer Science, and Statistics Home Openings : 1 Description Position Details: Gustavus Adolphus College invites applications for a tenure-track position of Assistant Professor in the Department of Mathematics, Computer Science, and Statistics to begin August 15, 2027. Employment Type: Full-Time (1.0 FTE), Benefits-Eligible; Exempt (Salaried) Prerequisites Required Qualifications: PhD in statistics, biostatistics, or closely related field At least one year of both theoretical and applied statistics coursework at the master’s level or higher Proficiency in R/RStudio, SAS, or Python Previous teaching experience Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated effectiveness in teaching Evidence of a commitment to undergraduate student advising Demonstrated commitment to supporting students from varied backgrounds and identities Evidence of preparation for primary teaching responsibilities as listed below Ability to conduct research or scholarly collaborations with undergraduates Interest in, and preparation for, leadership roles in the college and profession Things you will do: Gustavus faculty teach, advise, conduct research, and serve the college and department. Teach a 6-course equivalent each academic year. In their first year, the successful candidate will receive a reduced teaching assignment of five courses, plus one fully-compensated course release. Courses may be different sections of the same course within a semester. Primary teaching responsibilities will include teaching a wide range of statistics courses , and contributions to general education. Help cultivate a welcoming community where everyone feels a sense of belonging. We strive to foster an environment where people can be themselves, build community, learn, and grow. Elevate your teaching by joining a teaching circle, participating in workshops, applying for an internal teaching development grant, and engaging in conversations about teaching with colleagues across campus. Advance your scholarship by working with undergraduate research assistants, joining a writing retreat, applying for an internal grant, receiving travel funds to present at conferences, receiving help applying for external grants, and making use of our research facilities. Develop professional skills by participating in faculty meetings and committees, attending faculty development days, and taking advantage of the College’s membership to the National Center for Faculty Development and Diversity (NCFDD). How to apply: Visit https://gustavus.edu/jobs/ and complete the online application. The documents that must be uploaded include the following: Letter of application that addresses the required and preferred position qualifications Curriculum vitae A brief (one page) statement of teaching philosophy If not provided in your CV, a list of previous teaching experiences including courses taught, your role (e.g., lab instructor, standalone instructor) and what statistical software was used (if applicable) Describe your approach to teaching undergraduate students Describe how you work with students from varied quantitative backgrounds A brief statement of scholarship (two pages maximum) in which you describe: Your current area(s) of scholarship Your plan for scholarship during the pre-tenure period How you would involve undergraduates in your scholarship For candidates whose PhD is not in statistics or biostatistics, a brief statement (one page maximum) in which you describe how your coursework and previous experiences have prepared you for this position Transcripts (scanned copies acceptable) The names and contact information for three professional references (at least one must be able to address teaching experience and teaching effectiveness; please indicate the teaching reference in your letter of application). Please do not ask references to submit letters of recommendation; the committee will conduct reference checks by phone. For full consideration, applications must be received by Friday, September 25, 2026. While applications may be accepted after this date, it is not guaranteed that they will be considered. At this time, please only upload the required documents listed above. Incomplete applications will not be considered by the search committee. Things you’ll like: Based on data from AAUP (American Association of University Professors) and CUPA (College and University Professional Association), we offer a competitive starting salary range of $66,000 to $72,000 for a 9-month academic year. Actual pay will be adjusted based on job-related factors permitted by law, such as experience, training, certifications/licensure, market factors, departmental budgets, and responsibility. In addition, Gustavus provides comprehensive benefits designed to support your personal and financial well-being, including: Medical insurance (which includes access to Nice Healthcare) as well as dental, vision, and life insurance Workplace accommodations for physical or mental health concerns Access to mental health apps Onsite health services Free parking, exercise classes, use of library and athletic facilities Paid parental leave (after one year of employment) Employer contribution to retirement savings plan (after one year of employment) Tuition scholarships for dependents Tuition benefit plan for employees and spouse Institution Information: Gustavus Adolphus College is one of the nation’s leading private liberal arts colleges serving 2,000 students, where faculty help equip students to lead purposeful lives and to act on the great challenges of our time. The College aspires to be a community of persons from diverse backgrounds who respect and affirm the dignity of all people. Gustavus is located on a scenic 340-acre hill in St. Peter, Minnesota, and within a short drive to the Minneapolis/Saint Paul and Mankato metro areas. Learn more at https://gustavus.edu/provost/newfaculty/ . Gustavus Adolphus College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, disability, religion, age, sexual orientation, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Department Information: The Department of Mathematics, Computer Science, and Statistics offers majors in Mathematics, Mathematics Teaching, Computer Science, and Statistics and graduates an average of 35 students per year. Among the 9 faculty, the department is home to three statisticians with varied research interests. In addition to the statistics major, the statistics minor is popular with students across campus, including those majoring in Economics, Finance, Management, Biology, Psychology and others. It is the philosophy of the Department that the skills of analytical thinking and logical argument, combined with the ability to communicate effectively, form the core of a solid liberal arts education in the mathematical sciences. For more information about the department, its faculty, students, and courses, please see the department website at https://gustavus.edu/mcs/ . NOTE: Candidates will not be compensated for materials prepared as part of the interview process, and the College will not retain the materials for its own use. Contact Laura Hildreth | lhildreth@gustavus.edu | 507-933-7481 Posted : Mon Jun 29, 2026 Apply Now 800 West College Avenue Saint Peter, MN 56082 507-933-8000 © 2026 Gustavus Adolphus College Careers Feedback Privacy Statement Title IX"
    },
    "https://gustavus.edu/employment/job/2392": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Specialty Open) - Nursing",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Specialty Open) - Nursing It appears you have javascript disabled. Please enable javascript to get the full experience of gustavus.edu Skip to Main Content Skip to Footer Sign In Gustavus Adolphus College Make Your Life Count Gustavus Adolphus College Assistant Professor (Specialty Open) Nursing Home Openings : 1 Description Position Details: Gustavus Adolphus College invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in the Department of Nursing. We are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in simulation and any of the following specialty areas: medical-surgical, maternal-child, or mental health nursing. We offer a flexible start date of either January 1, 2027, or August 15, 2027, depending on the availability of the successful candidate. Employment Type: Full-Time (1.0 FTE), Benefits-Eligible; Exempt (Salaried) Prerequisites Required Qualifications: Doctorate degree in nursing or a related field (PhD, DNP, or EdD) is preferred; but we will consider Master's prepared nurses with either a doctorate in progress (please indicate anticipated completion date if in progress) or who will work toward completion of their doctorate degree during employment. (NOTE: A doctorate degree is required for tenure nomination, usually in the fifth year. Candidates without the earned doctorate will be hired at the rank of Instructor and will be eligible for support through the Gustavus Nursing Faculty Degree Completion Program.) Active registered nurse license (active Minnesota Registered Nurse licensure required at time of appointment) Demonstrated effectiveness in teaching Proficiency in conducting simulation-based learning and evaluation of clinical simulation Experience with curriculum development with simulation, using best educational pedagogy, and/or instructional design principles Current knowledge of patient simulation technologies. (i.e., proficiency with simulators and simulation software, AV equipment, electronic health records, and standardized patients) Strong communication and organizational skills Demonstrated commitment to supporting students from diverse backgrounds and identities Preferred Qualifications: Teaching experience at the undergraduate level Simulation certification completed or in process 5+ years of recent clinical experience in nursing Experience with nursing program assessment, evaluation, and accreditation activities Evidence of a commitment to undergraduate student advising Things you will do: Gustavus faculty teach, advise, conduct research, and serve the college and department. Teach a 6-course equivalent each academic year. In their first year, the successful candidate will receive a reduced teaching assignment of five courses, plus one fully-compensated course release. Primary teaching responsibilities will include a three course load in clinical simulation and medical surgical nursing, maternal newborn, or mental health courses. This position will work with all faculty to create, revise, and update simulation activities in the curriculum and maintain standards of operation and implementation of all simulation throughout the curriculum. In addition, this position will contribute to other nursing curriculum courses and potential future contributions to general education. The successful candidate will join college and departmental efforts to develop equitable pedagogies and inclusive cultures. This includes, but is not limited to, advising nursing majors and contributing to nursing department assessment, evaluation, and accreditation activities. Help cultivate a welcoming community where everyone feels a sense of belonging. We strive to foster an environment where people can be themselves, build community, learn, and grow. Elevate your teaching by joining a teaching circle, participating in workshops, applying for an internal teaching development grant, and engaging in conversations about teaching with colleagues across campus. Advance your scholarship by working with undergraduate research assistants, joining a writing retreat, applying for an internal grant, receiving travel funds to present at conferences, receiving help applying for external grants, and making use of our research facilities. Develop professional skills by participating in faculty meetings and committees, attending faculty development days, and taking advantage of the College’s membership to the National Center for Faculty Development and Diversity (NCFDD). How to apply: Visit https://gustavus.edu/jobs/ and complete the online application. The documents that must be uploaded include the following: Letter of application that addresses the required and preferred position qualifications Curriculum vitae A brief (one page) statement of teaching philosophy A brief (one page) statement of research interests A brief (one page) statement in which you describe how your lived experiences and/or activities in primary areas of responsibility (e.g., teaching, scholarship, service, and advising) contribute to diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging A brief (one page) statement of experience with simulation (specify creation, implementation, and evaluation of simulation education and experience with simulation technology) Transcripts (scanned copies acceptable) The names and contact information for three professional references (at least one must be able to address teaching experience and teaching effectiveness; please indicate the teaching reference in your letter of application). Please do not ask references to submit letters of recommendation; the committee will conduct reference checks by phone. For full consideration, applications must be received by August 15, 2026. While applications may be accepted after this date, it is not guaranteed that they will be considered. At this time, please only upload the required documents listed above; finalists may be asked to submit publications, syllabi, and/or student evaluations. Incomplete applications will not be considered by the search committee. Things you’ll like: Based on data from AAUP (American Association of University Professors) and CUPA (College and University Professional Association), we offer a competitive starting salary range of $70,000 to $76,000 for a 9-month academic year. Actual pay will be adjusted based on job-related factors permitted by law, such as experience, training, certifications/licensure, market factors, departmental budgets, and responsibility. In addition, Gustavus provides comprehensive benefits designed to support your personal and financial well-being, including: Medical insurance (which includes access to Nice Healthcare) as well as dental, vision, and life insurance Workplace accommodations for physical or mental health concerns Access to mental health apps Onsite health services Free parking, exercise classes, use of library and athletic facilities Paid parental leave (after one year of employment) Employer contribution to retirement savings plan (after one year of employment) Tuition scholarships for dependents Tuition benefit plan for employees and spouse Institution Information: Gustavus Adolphus College is one of the nation’s leading private liberal arts colleges serving 2,000 students, where faculty help equip students to lead purposeful lives and to act on the great challenges of our time. The College aspires to be a community of persons from diverse backgrounds who respect and affirm the dignity of all people. Gustavus is located on a scenic 340-acre hill in St. Peter, Minnesota, and within a short drive to the Minneapolis/Saint Paul and Mankato metro areas. Learn more at https://gustavus.edu/provost/newfaculty/ . Gustavus Adolphus College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, disability, religion, age, sexual orientation, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Department Information: The Department of Nursing fosters the development of nursing professionals who demonstrate the values of excellence, community, justice, service, and faith through cognitive practice, integration of learning, ethical reflection, and intercultural understanding. Gustavus Nursing graduates are distinguished by: synthesis and application of a liberal arts education to provide holistic care; ethical and reflective practice to promote a just and peaceful world; the ability to advocate for the health and wellbeing of all people; and a commitment to lifelong learning, leadership, and service to others. The Department of Nursing shares in the mission of the College through an innovative and dynamic education that embraces the highest standards of teaching and scholarship. For more information about the department, its faculty, students, and courses, please see the department website at https://gustavus.edu/nursing/ . Contact Jessica Stadick | jstadick@gustavus.edu | 507-933-6126 Posted : Wed May 20, 2026 Apply Now 800 West College Avenue Saint Peter, MN 56082 507-933-8000 © 2026 Gustavus Adolphus College Careers Feedback Privacy Statement Title IX"
    },
    "https://gustavus.edu/employment/job/2444": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Experimental Physics) - Physics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Experimental Physics) - Physics It appears you have javascript disabled. Please enable javascript to get the full experience of gustavus.edu Skip to Main Content Skip to Footer Sign In Gustavus Adolphus College Make Your Life Count Gustavus Adolphus College Assistant Professor (Experimental Physics) Physics Home Openings : 1 Description Position Details: Gustavus Adolphus College invites applications for a tenure-track position of Assistant Professor in the Department of Physics to begin August 15, 2027. Employment Type: Full-Time (1.0 FTE), Benefits-Eligible; Exempt (Salaried) Prerequisites Required Qualifications: PhD in an experimental sub-field of physics; we will consider candidates who have achieved ABD status and who will complete their degree by September 30, 2027 Evidence of effectiveness in teaching and commitment to undergraduate education in support of the mission of Gustavus Evidence of commitment to student advising, recruiting, or mentoring students from all backgrounds and identities Evidence of broad exposure to and skill with modern research-grade instrumentation Ability to develop an independent and sustainable experimental physics research program that is appropriate for the inclusion of undergraduate collaborators Preferred Qualifications: While the experimental sub-field of physics is open, some preference will be given to the candidate who is involved in optics or who can make meaningful use of the existing extensive optical infrastructure available at Gustavus Experience teaching undergraduate physics courses. Experience working with people from diverse backgrounds and a demonstrated commitment to pedagogical methods that enable all students to reach their maximum potential. Experience teaching or developing innovative instructional upper-level undergraduate labs utilizing modern research-grade instrumentation Experience conducting experimental physics research with undergraduate students Things you will do: Gustavus faculty teach, advise, conduct research, and serve the college and department. Teach a 6-course equivalent each academic year (typically two courses and associated lab(s) for a total of 12 contact hours per semester). In their first year, the successful candidate will receive a reduced teaching assignment of five courses, plus one fully-compensated course release. Primary teaching responsibilities will include undergraduate physics at all levels (introductory through upper-level courses) as well as dedicated courses for students from cognate science departments and for those students seeking exposure to physics through a general education experience. Work collaboratively with existing faculty to reimagine and redesign the upper-level physics laboratory sequence into a coherent, rigorous, and integrated laboratory experience that utilizes research-grade instrumentation suitable for a twenty-first century education. Develop an appropriate and independent experimental undergraduate physics research program (preferably on-campus) that will be sustainable and, in time, be capable of securing external funding and producing results that lead to peer-reviewed scientific publications. Actively participate in undergraduate student advising and mentoring. Help cultivate a welcoming community where everyone feels a sense of belonging. We strive to foster an environment where people can be themselves, build community, learn, and grow. Elevate your teaching by joining a teaching circle, participating in workshops, applying for an internal teaching development grant, and engaging in conversations about teaching with colleagues across campus. Advance your scholarship by working with undergraduate research assistants, joining a writing retreat, applying for an internal grant, receiving travel funds to present at conferences, receiving help applying for external grants, and making use of our research facilities. Develop professional skills by participating in faculty meetings and committees, attending faculty development days, and taking advantage of the College’s membership to the National Center for Faculty Development and Diversity (NCFDD). How to apply: Visit https://gustavus.edu/jobs/ and complete the online application. The documents that must be uploaded include the following: Letter of application that addresses the required and preferred position qualifications Curriculum vitae A brief (one to two page) statement of teaching philosophy that also addresses your ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds A brief (one to two page) experimental research plan appropriate for an undergraduate institution Transcripts (scanned copies acceptable) Three confidential professional letters of reference to be emailed to g-physicssearch2026@gustavus.edu . At least one reference letter should speak about the candidate’s teaching experience or potential, including the application of pedagogical methods that benefit all students and, where applicable, the candidate’s involvement with upper-level undergraduate physics labs. Additionally, at least one letter should address the candidate’s potential to conduct independent experimental physics research and their facility with modern research-grade instrumentation. Please specify which professional reference will speak to teaching potential and which to research potential. Reference letter writers may also be contacted by phone. For full consideration, applications must be received by October 12, 2026. While applications may be accepted after this date, it is not guaranteed that they will be considered. At this time, please only upload the required documents listed above; finalists will be asked to submit any additional information as needed. Incomplete applications will not be considered by the search committee. Things you’ll like: Based on data from AAUP (American Association of University Professors) and CUPA (College and University Professional Association), we offer a competitive starting salary range of $66,000 to $72,000 for a 9-month academic year. Actual pay will be adjusted based on job-related factors permitted by law, such as experience, training, certifications/licensure, market factors, departmental budgets, and responsibility. In addition, Gustavus provides comprehensive benefits designed to support your personal and financial well-being, including: Medical insurance (which includes access to Nice Healthcare) as well as dental, vision, and life insurance Workplace accommodations for physical or mental health concerns Access to mental health apps Onsite health services Free parking, exercise classes, use of library and athletic facilities Paid parental leave (after one year of employment) Employer contribution to retirement savings plan (after one year of employment) Tuition scholarships for dependents Tuition benefit plan for employees and spouse Institution Information: Gustavus Adolphus College is one of the nation’s leading private liberal arts colleges serving 2,000 students, where faculty help equip students to lead purposeful lives and to act on the great challenges of our time. The College aspires to be a community of persons from diverse backgrounds who respect and affirm the dignity of all people. Gustavus is located on a scenic 340-acre hill in St. Peter, Minnesota, and within a short drive to the Minneapolis/Saint Paul and Mankato metro areas. Learn more at https://gustavus.edu/provost/newfaculty/ . Gustavus Adolphus College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, disability, religion, age, sexual orientation, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Department Information: The Department of Physics seeks to provide an intellectual environment by cultivating an engaged community of scholars. We aim to challenge students to pursue an understanding of the natural world through the study of physics to develop scientifically-minded citizens and competent scientists. We aspire for our students to appreciate interdisciplinary perspectives and problem-solving approaches, and to communicate effectively with a variety of audiences. Overall, we aim to value and support the development of all members of our community. For more information about the department, its faculty, students, and courses, please see the department website at https://gustavus.edu/physics/ . NOTE: Candidates will not be compensated for materials prepared as part of the interview process, and the College will not retain the materials for its own use. Posted Sept. 14, 2026 Contact Paul Saulnier | psaul@gustavus.edu | 507-933-6123 Posted : Thu Oct 1, 2026 Apply Now 800 West College Avenue Saint Peter, MN 56082 507-933-8000 © 2026 Gustavus Adolphus College Careers Feedback Privacy Statement Title IX"
    },
    "https://gustavus.edu/employment/job/2432": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Acting and Directing) - Theatre and Dance",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Acting and Directing) - Theatre and Dance It appears you have javascript disabled. Please enable javascript to get the full experience of gustavus.edu Skip to Main Content Skip to Footer Sign In Gustavus Adolphus College Make Your Life Count Gustavus Adolphus College Assistant Professor (Acting and Directing) Theatre and Dance Home Openings : 1 Description Position Details: Gustavus Adolphus College invites applications for a tenure-track position of Assistant Professor in the Department of Theatre and Dance to begin August 15, 2027. Employment Type: Full-Time (1.0 FTE), Benefits-Eligible; Exempt (Salaried) Prerequisites Required Qualifications: Terminal degree (MFA or PhD) in Acting, Directing, or appropriately related theatre discipline; we will consider candidates who will complete their degree by September 30, 2027 Evidence of a body of work as a professional actor and/or director Evidence of teaching experience Commitment to advising and mentoring undergraduate students Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated effectiveness in teaching Demonstrated commitment to supporting students from varied backgrounds and identities A broad knowledge of acting and directing techniques Evidence of post-secondary teaching experience Things you will do: Gustavus faculty teach, advise, conduct research, and serve the college and department. Teach a 6-course equivalent each academic year. In their first year, the successful candidate will receive a reduced teaching assignment of five courses, plus one fully-compensated course release. Courses may be different sections of the same course within a semester. Primary teaching responsibilities will include Acting and Performance levels 1 through 3, World Theatre Analysis, and Directing 1, and contributions to general education. Direct one main stage production each semester. Directing assignments are factored into the faculty members teaching load and receive equivalent course releases. Mentor students in performance and professional development, and advise students within the Theatre and Dance degree plans. Help cultivate a welcoming community where everyone feels a sense of belonging. We strive to foster an environment where people can be themselves, build community, learn, and grow. Elevate your teaching by joining a teaching circle, participating in workshops, applying for an internal teaching development grant, and engaging in conversations about teaching with colleagues across campus. Advance your scholarship by working with undergraduate research assistants, joining a writing retreat, applying for an internal grant, receiving travel funds to present at conferences, receiving help applying for external grants, and making use of our research facilities. Develop professional skills by participating in faculty meetings and committees, attending faculty development days, and taking advantage of the College’s membership to the National Center for Faculty Development and Diversity (NCFDD). How to apply: Visit https://gustavus.edu/jobs/ and complete the online application. The documents that must be uploaded include the following: Letter of application that addresses the required and preferred position qualifications Curriculum vitae A brief (one page) statement of teaching philosophy A brief (one page) statement in which you describe how your activities in primary areas of responsibility (e.g., teaching, scholarship and creativity, service, and advising) help cultivate a welcoming community where every student feels a sense of belonging Transcripts (scanned copies acceptable) The names and contact information for three professional references (at least one must be able to address teaching experience and teaching effectiveness; please indicate the teaching reference in your letter of application). Please do not ask references to submit letters of recommendation; the committee will conduct reference checks by phone. For full consideration, applications must be received by September 11, 2026. While applications may be accepted after this date, it is not guaranteed that they will be considered. At this time, please only upload the required documents listed above; finalists may be asked to submit additional materials as needed. Incomplete applications will not be considered by the search committee. Things you’ll like: Based on data from AAUP (American Association of University Professors) and CUPA (College and University Professional Association), we offer a competitive entry-level starting salary range of $62,000 to $68,000 for a 9-month academic year. Appointment and starting salary will be fixed at the Assistant Professor level based on institutional budget and standard rank placement. In addition, Gustavus provides comprehensive benefits designed to support your personal and financial well-being, including: Medical insurance (which includes access to Nice Healthcare) as well as dental, vision, and life insurance Workplace accommodations for physical or mental health concerns Access to mental health apps Onsite health services Free parking, exercise classes, use of library and athletic facilities Paid parental leave (after one year of employment) Employer contribution to retirement savings plan (after one year of employment) Tuition scholarships for dependents Tuition benefit plan for employees and spouse Institution Information: Gustavus Adolphus College is one of the nation’s leading private liberal arts colleges serving 2,000 students, where faculty help equip students to lead purposeful lives and to act on the great challenges of our time. The College aspires to be a community of persons from diverse backgrounds who respect and affirm the dignity of all people. Gustavus is located on a scenic 340-acre hill in St. Peter, Minnesota, and within a short drive to the Minneapolis/Saint Paul and Mankato metro areas. Learn more at https://gustavus.edu/provost/newfaculty/ . Gustavus Adolphus College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, disability, religion, age, sexual orientation, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Department Information: The Theatre and Dance Department mission emphasizes the value of performance as a vital means of working for social justice and personal transformation. The Department mentors majors and non-majors alike in explorations of the many ways theatre and dance artists interpret and affect society. For more information about the department, its faculty, students, and courses, please see the department website at https://gustavus.edu/academics/departments/theatre-and-dance . NOTE: Candidates will not be compensated for materials prepared as part of the interview process, and the College will not retain the materials for its own use. Contact Jared Land | jland@gustavus.edu | 507-933-7353 Posted : Fri Aug 7, 2026 Apply Now 800 West College Avenue Saint Peter, MN 56082 507-933-8000 © 2026 Gustavus Adolphus College Careers Feedback Privacy Statement Title IX"
    },
    "https://gustavus.edu/employment/job/2448": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Donor Relations - Advancement",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Donor Relations - Advancement It appears you have javascript disabled. Please enable javascript to get the full experience of gustavus.edu Skip to Main Content Skip to Footer Sign In Gustavus Adolphus College Make Your Life Count Gustavus Adolphus College Assistant Director of Donor Relations Advancement Home Openings : 1 Description JOB SUMMARY: Direct, lead, and develop the comprehensive plan and implementation of stewardship and recognition for donors to Gustavus. This includes development and advancement of programs, events, procedures, budgets, and materials that assure accurate, timely, and appropriate tracking and interaction between the College, its donors and prospective donors, in an effort to strengthen relationships and achieve fundraising goals. Cultivate a donor-centric environment of gratitude and appreciation by communicating and demonstrating the impact of philanthropic support and inspiring alumni, parents, and friends to support the College to their fullest potential. Employment Type: Full-Time (1.0 FTE), Exempt (Salaried), Benefits-Eligible Salary Range: $54,000-$60,000 annually How to apply: Continue here or visit https://gustavus.edu/jobs/ to complete the online application and submit a resume and cover letter. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. MAIN RESPONSIBILITIES: Stewardship Program Development and Management Design, implement, and manage a comprehensive donor relations and stewardship program that aligns with the College’s strategic plan and Advancement’s goals. Develop and maintain a framework for donor recognition and engagement, ensuring consistent, personalized, and meaningful interactions across all giving levels. Assess, refine, and maintain stewardship policies, procedures, and best practices. Drive departmental and campus-wide implementation. Donor Recognition and Events Orchestrate a streamlined, personalized system for expressing gratitude from students, faculty, and executive leadership to donors, ensuring both timely and impactful acknowledgments. Optimize recognition practices and engagement opportunities for existing and future Giving Societies. Lead signage efforts to recognize donor generosity. Coordinate with Facilities, Marketing, and external vendors to design, produce, and install all recognition on campus. Partner with College leadership to conceptualize and produce strategic stewardship and campaign events that cultivate relationships with constituents, supporters, and major donor prospects. Drive the end-to-end planning of receptions, luncheons, dinners, dedications, groundbreakings, grand-openings, athletics suite hosting, and other events ensuring positive experiences. Represent donor stewardship at Advancement’s Leadership meetings and work closely with Gift Planners, Advancement Services, Prospect Research, Planned Giving, Annual Fund, and Alumni and Parent Engagement to ensure the holistic approach to a donor’s philanthropic journey. Donor Communications Oversee the creation and distribution of all stewardship materials highlighting donor impact. Develop and design strategic donor-targeted marketing material and language content related to funds and programs. Coordinate with departments across campus to build articulate, compelling, and visually appealing cases for support of Gustavus projects and programs. Partner with the Marketing and Communication department to ensure materials and stories are available to steward and inspire donors. Collaboration and Relationship Building Build and maintain strong relationships with donors, providing exceptional customer service and fostering meaningful engagement that strengthens relationships with the College's donors. Collaborate with Gift Planners for pre-solicit gift agreement concepts and gift instrument development for endowed and current restricted gifts. Ensure that departments across the College are aware of relevant donor expectations, and donors are appropriately updated on use of gifted funds. Cultivate and strengthen rapport with various offices and academic departments across campus. Represent Advancement in cross-divisional efforts, as it relates to donor stewardship and donor intent for fund use. Engage proactively with key partners in the Office of the President, Provost, Finance, Marketing and Financial Aid. Manage the stewardship budget and provide leaders and budget officers throughout the College with support related to donor-restricted funding in their budgets. Strategic Planning Engagement Contribute to the development of Advancement’s strategic framework as a key member of the team and offer long-term visioning to build a culture of philanthropy. Remain current on best practices within donor relations and stewardship and bring creative expertise and innovative approaches to the directional planning process that go beyond traditional thinking. Other duties as assigned and observed. Prerequisites MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor's degree in a related field. Proven experience and success in non-profit development and/or donor relations preferred. Computer literacy and knowledge of Google, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint is required. Experience with databases is a plus, especially Slate for Advancement. Must have demonstrated ability to organize and manage multiple projects creatively and flexibly. Must have the ability to forge strong working relationships and have the desire to work as part of a team. Must have the capacity for building confidence and trust among alumni, parents, and friends of Gustavus Adolphus College and have the ability to maintain a high level of confidentiality. Must be self-motivated and organized, with strong attention to accuracy. Exceptional oral and written communication skills. Must have the ability to participate in occasional evening and weekend activities. Experience in planning upscale events for small and large audiences is preferred. Gustavus offers competitive and comprehensive benefits which include: Medical insurance (which includes access to Nice Healthcare) as well as dental, vision, and life insurance Workplace accommodations for physical or mental health concerns Onsite health services Free parking, exercise classes, and use of library and athletic facilities Paid parental leave Employer contribution to retirement savings plan (after one year of employment) Tuition scholarships for dependents Tuition benefit plan for employees and spouse 13 paid Holidays + generous PTO plan Gustavus Adolphus College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, disability, religion, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Gustavus Adolphus College is one of the nation’s leading private liberal arts colleges serving approximately 1,800 students. The College aspires to be a community of persons from diverse backgrounds who respect and affirm the dignity of all people. Known for its strong science, writing, music, athletics, study-away, and service-learning programs, Gustavus is located on a scenic 340-acre hill in St. Peter, Minnesota only one hour southwest of the Twin Cities. Contact Annie Escalera | aescalara@gustavus.edu | 507-933-6513 Posted : Tue Sep 29, 2026 Apply Now 800 West College Avenue Saint Peter, MN 56082 507-933-8000 © 2026 Gustavus Adolphus College Careers Feedback Privacy Statement Title IX"
    },
    "https://gustavus.edu/employment/job/2352": {
      "title": "Custodian - Custodial and Support Services",
      "description": "Custodian - Custodial and Support Services It appears you have javascript disabled. Please enable javascript to get the full experience of gustavus.edu Skip to Main Content Skip to Footer Sign In Gustavus Adolphus College Make Your Life Count Gustavus Adolphus College Custodian Custodial and Support Services Home Openings : 1 Description Gustavus Adolphus College invites applications for our Custodian positions in the Custodial and Support Services Department. Employment Type: Full-time (1.0 FTE), Non-exempt (Hourly), Benefits-Eligible Shift: Monday - Friday, 5am-1pm Wage Range: $15.00-$16.50 MAIN RESPONSIBILITIES: Properly cleans and maintains multiple areas on campus, as assigned Shampooing carpets, waxing floors, polishing glass, emptying trash, recycling, compost Maintaining floors, cleaning wood, linoleum, tile, and other flooring types Report’s maintenance concerns via work order request to appropriate personnel Collaborates with other CSS staff, leads, and supervisors to complete daily tasks Prerequisites MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: High school diploma or equivalent Must be able to lift up to 50 pounds and stand for up to 8 hours per day Previous experience in cleaning and/or custodial services Must be a self-starter and able to produce work with minimum supervision Demonstrated ability to build positive working relationships Strong communication skills and positive demeanor Gustavus offers competitive and comprehensive benefits which include: Medical, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance Short-Term Disability Parental Leave Gustavus contribution to retirement savings plan after one year of employment Free: Parking, exercise classes, use of library and athletic facilities Tuition options for dependents after two year of employment Tuition benefit plan for employees and spouse 13 paid Holidays + generous PTO plan Application Procedures: To apply for this position, please continue the process on our website, www.gustavus.edu/humanresources/employment to complete the online application. Submit a resume if available. Gustavus Adolphus College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, disability, religion, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Gustavus Adolphus College is one of the nation’s leading private liberal arts colleges serving approximately 1,800 students. The College aspires to be a community of persons from diverse backgrounds who respect and affirm the dignity of all people. Known for its strong science, writing, music, athletics, study-away, and service-learning programs, Gustavus is located on a scenic 340-acre hill in St. Peter, Minnesota only one hour southwest of the Twin Cities. Contact Nick Ross | ross@gustavus.edu | 507-933-7643 Posted : Mon Jan 5, 2026 Apply Now 800 West College Avenue Saint Peter, MN 56082 507-933-8000 © 2026 Gustavus Adolphus College Careers Feedback Privacy Statement Title IX"
    },
    "https://gustavus.edu/employment/job/2445": {
      "title": "Associate Dean of Students - Dean of Students",
      "description": "Associate Dean of Students - Dean of Students It appears you have javascript disabled. Please enable javascript to get the full experience of gustavus.edu Skip to Main Content Skip to Footer Sign In Gustavus Adolphus College Make Your Life Count Gustavus Adolphus College Associate Dean of Students Dean of Students Home Openings : 1 Description JOB SUMMARY: The Associate Dean of Students provides leadership within the Student Life Division while serving as a key resource for student support, care coordination, advocacy, and retention. This role supervises departments and professional staff, supports students navigating complex personal, academic, and institutional challenges, and leads initiatives that promote student wellbeing, engagement, belonging, and persistence. The Associate Dean also contributes to divisional strategy, crisis response, budget management, staff development, and campus-wide student success initiatives. Employment Status: Full-Time (1.0 FTE), Exempt (Salaried), Benefits Eligible Salary Range: $70,000-85,000 How to apply: Continue here or visit https://gustavus.edu/jobs/ to complete the online application and submit a resume and cover letter. Applications will be reviewed beginning October 15, 2026. MAIN RESPONSIBILITIES Student Support, Care Coordination & Retention: Direct Student Support: Serve as the dean for assigned cohorts, providing direct student support, general counseling, advocacy, care-mapping, and problem-solving services to students and their families. Student Support Specialist & Case Management: Act as a Student Support Specialist / Case Manager within the Dean of Students office to deliver coordinated care, navigation, and wrap-around support for students facing complex personal, academic, or institutional challenges. Basic Needs & Wellness Integration: Lead the integration of basic needs resources (housing/food security, emergency support) with holistic wellness initiatives; serve as a primary liaison connecting students with the Counseling Center, Health Service, and community resources. Retention Focus & Engagement Opportunities: Develop, assess, and implement targeted retention strategies and student engagement opportunities designed to foster connection, sense of belonging, and persistence, particularly for students identified as at-risk or navigating significant barriers. Care Mapping & Team Collaboration: Conduct individual care-mapping sessions with students to outline actionable growth pathways; actively serve on multi-disciplinary support groups including the Student Assistance Team, Behavioral Assessment Team, and Bias Response Team. Leadership, Supervision & Operations: Departmental Supervision: Supervise and support multiple departments within the Student Life Division. Personnel Development: Manage professional staff recruitment, orientation, ongoing development, and employee engagement initiatives, including chairing search committees. Budget Management: Oversee and manage operational budgets within areas of responsibility and provide support to budget managers in departments under direct supervision. Leadership Group: Serve as an active member of the Dean of Students leadership team and the Student Life Leadership Team, contributing to divisional strategy, crisis management, and student success initiatives. On-Call Responsibilities & Institutional Service: Crisis Response: Share responsibilities in the campus-wide Deans on-call rotation for 24/7/365 emergency and crisis response. Committee Service: Participate in designated divisional and College-wide committees, programs, and strategic planning activities. Awards & Honors: Administer the annual Student Life awards process—soliciting nominations, coordinating selection, and managing associated Honors Weekend events. Other Duties: Perform other duties as assigned. (Note: Some evening, weekend, and holiday work is required). Prerequisites MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: 3+ years in student-facing job function in a higher education setting Bachelor’s Degree in related field Ability to work occasional nights, weekends, holidays as needed to support the College Ability to measure success in overall results of work output PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Knowledge and understanding of the residential liberal arts college experience Masters Degree in relevant field WORK EXPECTATIONS: Must live within 20 miles of the Gustavus Adolphus College campus Expected to work primarily in person, on campus (potential remote work options at the discretion of the supervisor) Gustavus offers competitive and comprehensive benefits which include: Medical insurance (which includes access to Nice Healthcare) as well as dental, vision, and life insurance Workplace accommodations for physical or mental health concerns Onsite health services Free parking, exercise classes, and use of library and athletic facilities Paid parental leave Employer contribution to retirement savings plan (after one year of employment) Tuition scholarships for dependents Tuition benefit plan for employees and spouse 13 paid Holidays + generous PTO plan Gustavus Adolphus College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, disability, religion, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Gustavus Adolphus College is one of the nation’s leading private liberal arts colleges serving approximately 1,800 students. The College aspires to be a community of persons from diverse backgrounds who respect and affirm the dignity of all people. Known for its strong science, writing, music, athletics, study-away, and service-learning programs, Gustavus is located on a scenic 340-acre hill in St. Peter, Minnesota only one hour southwest of the Twin Cities. Contact Charlie Potts | cpotts@gustavus.edu | 507-933-7526 Posted : Tue Sep 22, 2026 Apply Now 800 West College Avenue Saint Peter, MN 56082 507-933-8000 © 2026 Gustavus Adolphus College Careers Feedback Privacy Statement Title IX"
    },
    "https://gustavus.edu/employment/job/2409": {
      "title": "Market Place Supervisor - Dining Service",
      "description": "Market Place Supervisor - Dining Service It appears you have javascript disabled. Please enable javascript to get the full experience of gustavus.edu Skip to Main Content Skip to Footer Sign In Gustavus Adolphus College Make Your Life Count Gustavus Adolphus College Market Place Supervisor Dining Service Home Openings : 1 Description JOB SUMMARY: This position is responsible for supervising the day-to-day operations of the Market Place and working as part of the Market Place leadership team. Employment Type: Full-time (1.0 FTE), Non-exempt (Hourly), Benefits-Eligible Schedule: Rotating shifts (morning/afternoon/evening) Monday - Friday, with one-two weekends a month Market Place hours of operation (may vary throughout the year): 7:00am-9:30pm Pay Range: $18.00-$20.00 per hour MAIN RESPONSIBILITIES: Operations and Maintenance Supervise the day-to-day operations of the Market Place. Ensure that service, sanitation, and food products meet quality standards. Monitor food and supply levels and coordinate orders for future service periods. Coordinate scheduled and emergency maintenance with service and production schedules and communicate updates to Dining Service staff. Maintain a neat and clean work environment and professional appearance. Maintain professional service standards as established by the Director and Assistant Director of Dining Service. Supervision and Training Train, supervise, and provide leadership and work direction to regular and student employees. Assist in the training, evaluation, and discipline of regular and student staff. Collaborate with the Assistant Director of Dining Service to provide input on scheduling of full-time, part-time, and student employees. Organize workflow and ensure employees understand assigned duties and delegated tasks. Serve as a positive role model for all Dining Service staff. Work through unit personnel to accomplish departmental goals and obligations. Team Collaboration and Customer Service Serve as back-fill support for any open stations within the Dining Center. Demonstrate the ability to work effectively in a team setting, including communication with student employees, supervisors, and other Dining Service staff members. Act as a communication link between Dining Service staff, customers, and the Assistant Director of Dining Service. Participate in planning meetings with department personnel and supervisory staff. Respond to and address customer feedback and concerns in a professional manner. Provide excellent customer service to all guests. Work as part of the Dining Service Management Team, participating in operational decision-making and supporting Catering/Concessions areas as requested. Try new methods and accept suggestions and direction for changes in procedures. All other duties as assigned. Prerequisites MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: High School Diploma or equivalent. Six months experience in a high volume dining service or restaurant or related experience. Strong customer service skills with the ability to create a welcoming and positive atmosphere. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to effectively lead and motivate a team. Proficiency in maintaining cleanliness and adhering to health and safety standards. Experience in a supervisory role within a food service environment, preferred. Additional Information: Physical requirements include the ability to stand for extended periods and lift moderate weights. This position has been designated as weather- or emergency-essential. In the event of a closure of the College, it is vital that you report to work if scheduled. You will receive regular pay for the hours normally scheduled to work that day plus your overtime rate at 1 ½ times your regular rate for the actual hours worked during the closing Application Procedures: To apply for this position, please continue the process on our website, www.gustavus.edu/humanresources/employment to complete the online application and submit a resume, if available. Gustavus offers competitive and comprehensive benefits which include: Medical insurance (which includes access to Nice Healthcare) as well as dental, vision, and life insurance Workplace accommodations for physical or mental health concerns Onsite health services Free parking, exercise classes, and use of library and athletic facilities Paid parental leave Employer contribution to retirement savings plan (after one year of employment) Tuition scholarships for dependents Tuition benefit plan for employees and spouse 13 paid Holidays + generous PTO plan Gustavus Adolphus College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, disability, religion, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Gustavus Adolphus College is one of the nation’s leading private liberal arts colleges serving approximately 1,800 students. The College aspires to be a community of persons from diverse backgrounds who respect and affirm the dignity of all people. Known for its strong science, writing, music, athletics, study-away, and service-learning programs, Gustavus is located on a scenic 340-acre hill in St. Peter, Minnesota only one hour southwest of the Twin Cities. Contact Bobbi Sellner | bsellner@gustavus.edu | 507-933-7689 Posted : Wed May 27, 2026 Apply Now 800 West College Avenue Saint Peter, MN 56082 507-933-8000 © 2026 Gustavus Adolphus College Careers Feedback Privacy Statement Title IX"
    },
    "https://gustavus.edu/employment/job/2446": {
      "title": "Operating Engineer - Facilities",
      "description": "Operating Engineer - Facilities It appears you have javascript disabled. Please enable javascript to get the full experience of gustavus.edu Skip to Main Content Skip to Footer Sign In Gustavus Adolphus College Make Your Life Count Gustavus Adolphus College Operating Engineer Facilities Home Openings : 1 Description JOB SUMMARY: The Operating Engineer is responsible for the safe and efficient operation, maintenance, and monitoring of campus boilers, steam distribution systems, chillers, chilled water distribution systems, Building Management Systems (BMS), and all related auxiliary equipment, including air compressors, pumps, and HVAC components. This position ensures proper functioning of all heating, ventilation, and air conditioning (HVAC) systems across campus facilities. Employment Status: Full-Time (1.0 FTE), Benefits-Eligible, Non-Exempt (Hourly) Pay Range: $25.00-$30.00 per hour How to apply: Visit https://gustavus.edu/jobs/ to complete the online application and submit a resume. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Operate and oversee the operation of steam boilers and the steam distribution system in accordance with applicable codes and regulations. Operate and maintain campus chillers and chilled water distribution systems. Maintain and troubleshoot HVAC systems in all campus buildings. Inspect buildings and facilities to determine mechanical repair and maintenance needs. Assist the Chief Engineer in coordinating Heating Plant operations with other maintenance and repair personnel. Assist in scheduling and coordinating planned outages with campus stakeholders and mechanical contractors. Order, track, and maintain HVAC supply inventory; monitor Heating Plant expenditures. Maintain accurate records of labor, materials, time, and inventory. Review mechanical system plans for new construction during the design phase to ensure uniformity of equipment and standardization of campus systems. Prepare and submit work progress reports as required. Maintain a clean, safe, and organized work environment compliant with OSHA safety standards. Remain current with evolving equipment, technology, job responsibilities, and procedures. Provide professional and service?oriented customer service to all customers and campus constituents. This position has been designated as weather- or emergency-essential. In the event of a closure of the College, it is vital to report to work only if contacted by the supervisor. You will receive regular pay for the hours normally scheduled to work that day plus your overtime rate at 1 ½ times your regular rate for the actual hours worked during the closing. Other duties as assigned. Prerequisites MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Minnesota Operating Engineer First Class C License Minimum of 3 years’ experience in HVAC and boiler operations Ability to work rotating weekends and respond to emergency situations, as needed Collaborate effectively with Facilities maintenance department High School diploma or equivalent WORKING ENVIRONMENT : Exposure to outside weather conditions year-round. Interaction with potentially hazardous chemicals and equipment Work at heights, including ladders, scaffolding, and roofs. Frequent moderate to heavy physical effort, including lifting up to 75 lbs. Gustavus offers competitive and comprehensive benefits which include: Medical insurance (which includes access to Nice Healthcare) as well as dental, vision, and life insurance Workplace accommodations for physical or mental health concerns Onsite health services Free parking, exercise classes, and use of library and athletic facilities Paid parental leave Employer contribution to retirement savings plan (after one year of employment) Tuition scholarships for dependents Tuition benefit plan for employees and spouse 13 paid Holidays + generous PTO plan Gustavus Adolphus College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, disability, religion, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Gustavus Adolphus College is one of the nation’s leading private liberal arts colleges serving approximately 1,800 students. The College aspires to be a community of persons from diverse backgrounds who respect and affirm the dignity of all people. Known for its strong science, writing, music, athletics, study-away, and service-learning programs, Gustavus is located on a scenic 340-acre hill in St. Peter, Minnesota only one hour southwest of the Twin Cities. Contact Travis Jordan | tjordan@gustavus.edu | 507-933-7574 Posted : Tue Sep 15, 2026 Apply Now 800 West College Avenue Saint Peter, MN 56082 507-933-8000 © 2026 Gustavus Adolphus College Careers Feedback Privacy Statement Title IX"
    },
    "https://gustavus.edu/employment/job/2452": {
      "title": "Financial Planning and Analysis Manager - Finance",
      "description": "Financial Planning and Analysis Manager - Finance It appears you have javascript disabled. Please enable javascript to get the full experience of gustavus.edu Skip to Main Content Skip to Footer Sign In Gustavus Adolphus College Make Your Life Count Gustavus Adolphus College Financial Planning and Analysis Manager Finance Home Openings : 1 Description JOB SUMMARY: The Financial Planning and Analysis (FP&A) Manager leads the College’s budgeting, forecasting, and financial planning processes, providing data-driven insights to support strategic decision-making. This role partners closely with senior leadership to enhance financial transparency, improve operational efficiency, and ensure alignment between financial resources and institutional priorities. The FP&A Manager plays a key role in strengthening financial accountability and advancing the College’s long-term financial sustainability. This position reports to the CFO and does not currently have any direct reports. Employment Type: Full-Time (1.0 FTE), Exempt (Salaried), Benefits-Eligible Salary Range: $85,000-$105,000, based on qualifications and relevant experience. Candidates who meet or exceed the minimum qualifications are encouraged to apply. How to apply: Continue here or visit https://gustavus.edu/jobs/ to complete the online application and submit a resume and cover letter. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. MAIN RESPONSIBILITIES: Budget: Create and manage the development of the College-wide budget, collaborating closely with the the CFO/VP of Finance, Controller, President’s leadership team, Budget managers, and others. Provide ongoing analysis and reporting on budget vs. actual spending. Develop and deliver budget reports for senior leadership and department leaders, turning data into clear, innovative, and actionable information. Lead the presentations and discussions with various stakeholders throughout the college on budget, actual spending, forecasting, and other related topics to ensure that the views of representatives from across campus are captured and incorporated as appropriate into the planning process. Serve as a main conduit of information sharing with campus stakeholders. Manage the technical aspects of the budget within the College’s ERP system. Provide education and training on budget methodology, process and system. Financial Analysis: Enhance and manage the College’s forecasting model. Provide detailed forecasting reports with variance analysis. Lead scenario planning and financial modeling to support key institutional initiatives and long-term planning. Serve as a strategic partner to the CFO/VP of Finance and senior leadership. Develop models, metrics, reports, charts, and automated operational solutions where feasible.  Develop and maintain the College’s financial dashboard. Identify and implement opportunities to improve financial processes, reporting efficiency, and data integrity. Translate financial data into actionable insights and communications methods to support decision-making across the College. Additional Responsibilities: Participate on college committees providing business acumen. Assist with debt management supporting the CFO/Vice President of Finance and Controller during the capital financing process. Provide exemplary service to the role’s stakeholders, including both internal and external constituents. Provide coordination with the Advancement Division and Controller’s office to ensure endowment funds are appropriately moved, recorded, and released to the appropriate budgetary group. Support the development of information and slide decks for various Board of Trustees and subcommittee meetings, including the Institutional Resource Group (IRG), Budget Committee, Investment Committee, and other committees as requested. All other duties as assigned. Prerequisites MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Accounting, or related field. 5+ years of financial management experience, including knowledge of budget development and management. Comfort dealing with ambiguity and ability to analyze highly complex information. Skilled at developing financial reporting and modeling. Ability to develop and nurture strong collaborative internal and external business relationships and partnerships. Advanced written and oral communication skills. Skilled at organizing projects and seeing them through to completion. Excellent computer skills, including ERP systems, planning software, data mining, Microsoft Excel, and Microsoft PowerPoint. Able to act independently within the parameters of the position description in all areas of authority and responsibility, and appropriately represent the CFO/Vice President of Finance and the President’s Office with internal and external stakeholders. Ability to exercise good judgment and decisions in an expeditious manner. Proficient with Google Apps and Microsoft Office possessing the ability to learn upgrades and new programs, as needed. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Master’s degree in Business, Finance, Accounting, or related field. CPA license. Experience working for a non-profit or university environment. Gustavus offers competitive and comprehensive benefits which include: Medical insurance (which includes access to Nice Healthcare) as well as dental, vision, and life insurance Workplace accommodations for physical or mental health concerns Onsite health services Free parking, exercise classes, and use of library and athletic facilities Paid parental leave Employer contribution to retirement savings plan (after one year of employment) Tuition scholarships for dependents Tuition benefit plan for employees and spouse 13 paid Holidays + generous PTO plan Gustavus Adolphus College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, disability, religion, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Gustavus Adolphus College is one of the nation’s leading private liberal arts colleges serving approximately 1,800 students. The College aspires to be a community of persons from diverse backgrounds who respect and affirm the dignity of all people. Known for its strong science, writing, music, athletics, study-away, and service-learning programs, Gustavus is located on a scenic 340-acre hill in St. Peter, Minnesota only one hour southwest of the Twin Cities. Contact Tracy Hegapemene | tracyh@gustavus.edu | 507-933-7499 Posted : Tue Oct 6, 2026 Apply Now 800 West College Avenue Saint Peter, MN 56082 507-933-8000 © 2026 Gustavus Adolphus College Careers Feedback Privacy Statement Title IX"
    },
    "https://gustavus.edu/employment/job/2429": {
      "title": "Creative Director & Senior Designer - Marketing & Communication",
      "description": "Creative Director & Senior Designer - Marketing & Communication It appears you have javascript disabled. Please enable javascript to get the full experience of gustavus.edu Skip to Main Content Skip to Footer Sign In Gustavus Adolphus College Make Your Life Count Gustavus Adolphus College Creative Director & Senior Designer Marketing & Communication Home Openings : 1 Description Gustavus Adolphus College seeks an accomplished, strategically minded Creative Director & Senior Designer to lead creative direction across the institution. The successful candidate will demonstrate an ability and eagerness to dive into our creative and brand needs, helping us elevate our Gustavus identity and brand through design and marketing opportunities across our region. This position is key to furthering the College’s marketing and communication objectives, including student enrollment, engaging Alumni and donors, and amplifying the energy across campus. This is a newly created role for Gustavus — historically, brand standards were set by an outside agency and upheld internally through art direction and production design. This new position will set the creative vision in partnership with outside agencies and carry it through to concept development and design across numerous touchpoints, ensuring visual and strategic consistency that meets the College’s goals. Job Summary: The Creative Director & Senior Designer is both a hands-on designer and a creative leader. You will originate campaign concepts, set the visual and video vision for the institution, and ensure brand consistency across a wide range of outputs and partners. A typical year will include projects such as multi-channel campaigns, publications, display graphics and beyond, so digital and video design fluency is essential . This is not a production role; it's a role for someone who understands how design and creative fuel institutional goals like enrollment and advancement, and is confident in current creative and cultural trends to influence others. Employment Status: Full-Time (1.0 FTE), Exempt (Salaried), Benefits Eligible Salary Range: $65,000-$80,000 How to apply: Continue here or visit https://gustavus.edu/jobs/ to complete the online application and submit a resume and portfolio. A cover letter is optional. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. *Visa Sponsorship is not available for this position* Main Responsibilities: Creative Leadership & Brand Vision Lead, steward, and champion the Gustavus brand. Serve as the creative authority for Gustavus Adolphus College, setting and championing a unified creative vision across all brand expressions. Lead the development of campaign concepts from idea to execution, translating institutional priorities into compelling creative work in partnership with creative agencies. Establish and evolve visual identity and brand standards, building on and extending the foundation set by prior external agency partners. Act as a trusted creative partner to leadership and department leads across campus. Set the vision for video and motion content, ensuring it aligns with the broader brand and creative strategy. Design Direction & Quality Personally lead high-priority brand design work while directing the overall quality and consistency of design output across the team. Support visual identity for Gustavus.edu Review and approve creative work across marketing needs of other departments to ensure a cohesive brand experience. Maintain and evolve brand guidelines, templates, and creative systems that scale across departments and channels. Strategy & Business Impact Bring a discerning eye to every project, balancing craft with strategic intent. • Understand and articulate how creative and design decisions drive institutional outcomes, including enrollment, advancement, and brand awareness. • Partner with the CMO and marketing leadership to align creative output with broader marketing and institutional strategy. Contribute a strategic point of view to planning conversations, not just execution. Team & Vendor Support Support and provide creative direction to the social media, video, website, admission, and advancement teams, helping shape their work at a strategic and visual level. Manage relationships with outside creative vendors — agencies, production companies, and freelance talent — ensuring their output meets brand and quality standards and stays ahead of design, video, and cultural trends. Provide project coordination for design projects not managed by another member of the Marketing and Communication team. Work with print and mail services to ensure completion of designed pieces. • Serve as an active member of the Marketing and Communication team and work collaboratively to ensure an integrated approach to brand and positioning for the college. Other duties as assigned. Prerequisites Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Graphic Design, Visual Communication, Fine Arts, or a related field; equivalent professional experience considered. 7+ years of professional design experience, including experience leading brand or creative direction (agency, in-house, or a mix of both). A portfolio demonstrating strong conceptual thinking, campaign development, and design craft. Demonstrated experience setting or upholding brand standards across multiple channels and audiences. Experience directing or collaborating closely on video and motion content. • Excellent presentation and communication skills; ability to build trust and influence across departments without formal authority over them. Strategic thinker who can connect design decisions to business and institutional goals. Comfortable working cross-functionally in a collaborative, deadline-driven environment. Preferred Qualifications: Proficiency in Adobe Creative Suite Experience managing or directing external creative vendors, including agencies and production partners. Strong creative concepting skills for motion and video, with experience leading the creative vision and collaborating with outsourced motion designers through execution. Experience in higher education, nonprofit, or other mission-driven marketing environments. Experience building or maturing a creative function within an organization (rather than only working within an established one). Direct people-management experience. Experience mentoring or providing creative direction to social and video specialists. Schedule & Work Environment This is a hybrid position, with a mix of on-campus work and flexibility for remote work. Specific hybrid arrangements are established in coordination with the supervisor and subject to departmental needs. Gustavus offers competitive and comprehensive benefits which include: Medical insurance (which includes access to Nice Healthcare) as well as dental, vision, and life insurance Workplace accommodations for physical or mental health concerns Onsite health services Free parking, exercise classes, and use of library and athletic facilities Paid parental leave Employer contribution to retirement savings plan (after one year of employment) Tuition scholarships for dependents Tuition benefit plan for employees and spouse 13 paid Holidays + generous PTO plan Gustavus Adolphus College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, disability, religion, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Gustavus Adolphus College is one of the nation’s leading private liberal arts colleges serving approximately 1,800 students. The College aspires to be a community of persons from diverse backgrounds who respect and affirm the dignity of all people. Known for its strong science, writing, music, athletics, study-away, and service-learning programs, Gustavus is located on a scenic 340-acre hill in St. Peter, Minnesota only one hour southwest of the Twin Cities. Contact Kim Frisch | kfrisch@gustavus.edu | 507-933-7683 Posted : Thu Jul 30, 2026 Apply Now 800 West College Avenue Saint Peter, MN 56082 507-933-8000 © 2026 Gustavus Adolphus College Careers Feedback Privacy Statement Title IX"
    },
    "https://gustavus.edu/employment/job/2447": {
      "title": "Senior Director of Marketing - Marketing & Communication",
      "description": "Senior Director of Marketing - Marketing & Communication It appears you have javascript disabled. Please enable javascript to get the full experience of gustavus.edu Skip to Main Content Skip to Footer Sign In Gustavus Adolphus College Make Your Life Count Gustavus Adolphus College Senior Director of Marketing Marketing & Communication Home Openings : 1 Description Position Overview: Gustavus Adolphus College seeks a talented and seasoned Senior Director of Marketing to join our team. Marketing and Communication is led by a co-leadership model with a Chief Marketing Officer (CMO) and a Chief Communications Officer (CCO). This position sits within the CMO’s lane, responsible for the operational execution of brand, enrollment, and program marketing. It does not overlap with the communications functions led by the CCO, which include institutional voice, media relations, and executive communications. The Senior Director will oversee a team of approximately 3–4 staff, manage agency relationships, and lead the marketing strategy and execution that helps Gustavus cut through a competitive market, grow enrollment, and deepen engagement with key audiences across the region. Job Summary: This position is a key part of the marketing leadership team, working closely with the Chief Marketing Officer to align and manage daily marketing operations across brand, enrollment, and program marketing. You will shape how Gustavus is known to prospective and current students, families, alumni, donors, sponsors, and partners. Your mission is to build marketing principles and assets in an authentic way — differentiating Gustavus in a crowded market, elevating brand awareness in the Twin Cities region, and delivering measurable results that drive enrollment. Employment Type: Full-Time (1.0 FTE), Exempt (Salaried), Benefits-Eligible Pay Range: $80,000-$92,000 annually Location: On-site, St. Peter, Minnesota (hybrid flexibility available) Main Responsibilities: Leadership & Team Lead and develop a team of approximately 3–4 marketing and creative staff, fostering a culture of collaboration, accountability, and high performance. Work closely with the Chief Marketing Officer to build and safeguard the overall marketing strategy for Gustavus Adolphus College. Contribute to the Marketing & Communications team’s strategic goals, planning, and outcomes, partnering with the CCO’s communications team where initiatives intersect. Campaigns & Channels Manage owned and paid campaigns across digital, print, social, and out-of-home channels. Lead coordinated multi-channel marketing efforts targeting key audiences. Build and oversee cross-channel marketing plans and agency management for day-to-day and campaign efforts. Manage agency partnerships and vendor relationships; direct contracted work and track ongoing progress. Audience & Program Marketing Lead and execute marketing development for core institutional audiences, including Admissions, Financial Aid, Advancement, Alumni, Student Life, Athletics, Fine Arts, and the Provost’s office. Build strong working relationships with partners across college departments, elevating collective marketing effectiveness. Collaborate with the full Marketing & Communications team to ensure marketing work is aligned and streamlined across platforms. Brand, Budget & Measurement Steward the marketing budget, ensuring responsible allocation and clear ROI reporting. Champion brand standards and visual identity in marketing execution; partner with the CCO’s team on brand governance across the institution. Drive impact through tracked and managed KPIs; build regular performance dashboards and recaps for the CMO and leadership. Ensure all deliverables are achieved, documented, and measured. Other duties as assigned. Prerequisites Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in marketing, communications, or a related field. Minimum of 8 years of paid industry experience in marketing or a related field. Minimum of 4 years managing direct reports. Demonstrated experience working effectively and collaboratively with executive leaders and business partners. Proven track record managing and stewarding marketing budgets. Experience managing agency partnerships and directing contracted work. Proficiency in Google Workspace and/or MS Office; Adobe Creative Suite; photo and video editing tools. Experience with Content Management Systems (e.g., Drupal, WordPress). Experience with media tracking systems and building performance recaps to highlight KPIs and value. Demonstrated experience in digital and paid media (SEM, Meta Ads, programmatic, etc.). Excellent communication, collaboration, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work independently, take initiative, and manage projects from start to finish. Creative mindset with a keen eye for detail and brand consistency. Ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in higher education, nonprofit, or other mission-driven marketing environments. Experience with CRM and/or marketing automation platforms (e.g., Salesforce, HubSpot, Slate, Marketo). Familiarity with enrollment marketing, advancement/alumni engagement, or fundraising communications. Experience working in a co-leadership or matrixed organizational structure. Graduate degree in marketing, communications, business, or a related field. Gustavus offers competitive and comprehensive benefits which include: Medical insurance (which includes access to Nice Healthcare) as well as dental, vision, and life insurance Workplace accommodations for physical or mental health concerns Onsite health services Free parking, exercise classes, and use of library and athletic facilities Paid parental leave Employer contribution to retirement savings plan (after one year of employment) Tuition scholarships for dependents Tuition benefit plan for employees and spouse 13 paid Holidays + generous PTO plan Gustavus Adolphus College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, disability, religion, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Gustavus Adolphus College is one of the nation’s leading private liberal arts colleges serving approximately 1,800 students. The College aspires to be a community of persons from diverse backgrounds who respect and affirm the dignity of all people. Known for its strong science, writing, music, athletics, study-away, and service-learning programs, Gustavus is located on a scenic 340-acre hill in St. Peter, Minnesota only one hour southwest of the Twin Cities. Contact Kim Frisch | kfrisch@gustavus.edu | 507-933-7683 Posted : Wed Sep 23, 2026 Apply Now 800 West College Avenue Saint Peter, MN 56082 507-933-8000 © 2026 Gustavus Adolphus College Careers Feedback Privacy Statement Title IX"
    },
    "https://gustavus.edu/employment/job/2449": {
      "title": "Academic Administrative Assistant - Physics, MCS, HES, and Sports Management",
      "description": "Academic Administrative Assistant - Physics, MCS, HES, and Sports Management It appears you have javascript disabled. Please enable javascript to get the full experience of gustavus.edu Skip to Main Content Skip to Footer Sign In Gustavus Adolphus College Make Your Life Count Gustavus Adolphus College Academic Administrative Assistant Physics, MCS, HES, and Sports Management Home Openings : 1 Description Are you an organized, community-minded professional looking to make an impact in higher education? As an Academic Administrative Assistant, you will serve as the central hub of the Physics Department and the Mathematics, Computer Science, & Statistics Department housed in Olin Hall and the Department of Health & Exercise Science and the Sport Management Program in the Lund Center at Gustavus Adolphus College. You will not only manage daily operations but also act as a steward of departmental resources and a mentor to student workers. This role is ideal for someone who thrives in a vibrant campus environment and enjoys a diverse range of responsibilities from tracking budgets and planning events to supporting faculty research and student success. Employment Status: Full-Time (.85 FTE), Benefits-Eligible, Non-exempt (Hourly) 40 hours/week for 40 weeks/year during the academic year; 15 hours/week during the remaining 12 weeks over the summer Note : This position offers a distinct work-life balance, with summers off while maintaining full benefits eligibility. Pay Range: $18.50-20.50 per hour Application Procedure: Please continue the process below or on our website, www.gustavus.edu/humanresources/employment to complete the online application and submit your resume. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. MAIN RESPONSIBILITIES: Financial & Budgetary Management Coordinate with the Finance Office, faculty, department chairs, and program directors to manage and track the budget and spending of faculty, departments, and programs within the building. This includes compiling, tracking, and reconciling receipts for spending and conference travel, as well as providing monthly budget reviews. Maintain office supplies and equipment and help coordinate faculty travel. Student Mentorship & Supervision Interview, hire, train, and supervise a team of student employees, managing their schedules, establishing their tasks, and providing professional guidance. Monitor and process time reports and the student employment budget. Act as liaison between the department and the Student Employment Office regarding student employment agreements. Serve as a welcoming resource for students, assisting with administrative needs such as declaring majors or assigning advisors. Faculty Support Oversee general office procedures, including managing faculty schedules, directing visitors, and serving as the liaison with Facilities and Technology Services to ensure the physical space effectively supports teaching and learning. Orient new faculty to general policies, procedures, equipment, and campus resources; sets up offices for new faculty. Assist with the implementation of faculty searches. Communications & Event Coordination Lead the planning and execution of departmental events, including guest lectures, student gatherings, and special projects. Coordinate schedule for evening/weekend use of department/building hall and room assignments, as requested. Attend department meetings and record meeting minutes. Department-Specific Support Within Olin Hall, act as primary contact for building, classroom, restroom, common area, office, key, and equipment maintenance, upkeep, and safety, collaborating with Facilities, Campus Safety, Gustavus Technology Services, and the Office of the Registrar. Prerequisites MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: High School diploma or equivalent. 2+ years of administrative support or similar experience. Strong written and verbal communication skills. A demonstrated commitment to fostering an inclusive work environment and the ability to communicate effectively with diverse populations. Proficiency in Google Workspace and Microsoft Office Suite products. Experience managing and/or tracking a budget PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Associate’s degree or Bachelor’s degree. Experience in a higher education setting. Proficiency with creative tools for marketing (e.g., Canva) and social media management. Demonstrated ability in supervision and training (specifically student employment). Gustavus offers competitive and comprehensive benefits which include: Medical insurance (which includes access to Nice Healthcare) as well as dental, vision, and life insurance Workplace accommodations for physical or mental health concerns Onsite health services Free parking, exercise classes, and use of library and athletic facilities Paid parental leave Employer contribution to retirement savings plan (after one year of employment) Tuition scholarships for dependents Tuition benefit plan for employees and spouse 13 paid Holidays + generous PTO plan Gustavus Adolphus College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, disability, religion, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Gustavus Adolphus College is one of the nation’s leading private liberal arts colleges serving approximately 1,800 students. The College aspires to be a community of persons from diverse backgrounds who respect and affirm the dignity. Contact Jillian Downey | jdowney@gustavus.edu | 507-933-7634 Posted : Mon Sep 28, 2026 Apply Now 800 West College Avenue Saint Peter, MN 56082 507-933-8000 © 2026 Gustavus Adolphus College Careers Feedback Privacy Statement Title IX"
    }
  },
